\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces STREAM Triad bandwidth sweep, SSE2 vs.\ AVX2 builds. The two instruction sets are indistinguishable at every thread count: the kernel is bandwidth-bound, not vectorization-bound.}}{13}{figure.caption.16}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces ODE error vs.\ CPU time for the five methods, across both payoffs and grid sizes, reproducing Niesen--Wright Figure~1. The Krylov integrator dominates in the ${\sim }10^{-4}$ accuracy band; Crank--Nicolson's non-monotone stiff-mode ringing ($R(-\infty ) = -1$) is visible as predicted.}}{14}{figure.caption.19}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Cache-aware roofline for the two hot kernels at $n=31$ and $n=61$. At $n=61$ the SpMV has spilled to DRAM; the vertical distance from the measured point to the L3 roof at the same arithmetic intensity is exactly the traffic a matrix-powers reformulation would recover.}}{15}{figure.caption.25}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Per-kernel strong scaling at $n=31$ and $n=61$, both initialization arms. SpMV shows a plateau at $n=31$ and a superlinear transition at $n=61$; Gram--Schmidt shows the synchronization staircase.}}{17}{figure.caption.27}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Per-kernel weak-scaling efficiency $T(1)/T(P)$ with $n(P) = n_1 P^{1/3}$ rounded odd, cache-tier crossings annotated.}}{17}{figure.caption.28}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The $m(n)$ Krylov-growth curve, measured with the convergence check enabled and quarantined from the scaling instrument, which pins $m=8$.}}{18}{figure.caption.29}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces The locality control. Only \texttt {block} carries an aggregate bandwidth DRAM cannot supply, so the transition is genuinely L3 residency, not a scheduling coincidence.}}{19}{figure.caption.31}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Predicted vs.\ measured basis condition number and the certified block width $s_{\max }$ across the swept operator family.}}{21}{figure.caption.34}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces The confound control: $s_{\max }$ under pinned spectrum with varying $m$ (flat), and pinned $m$ with varying spectrum (4--14).}}{21}{figure.caption.35}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Reductions per Arnoldi cycle: MGS vs.\ the certified $s$-step arm.}}{22}{figure.caption.37}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces The log-robustness law: prediction error in decades vs.\ $\log _{10}\kappa (X)$. The rigorous bound is the identity line; the measured data grows logarithmically, with the constant-coefficient and variable-coefficient families fitted separately. The real Black--Scholes operator (test point, excluded from fits) sits under one $s$-step at every grid.}}{24}{figure.caption.40}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces The asset-dimension law: canonical $\kappa (X)$ grows geometrically in $d$ with an analytic slope; the dense value diverges from it exactly where the spectrum degenerates.}}{25}{figure.caption.43}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Gram--Schmidt wall-clock under the calibrated tree reduction vs.\ the $O(P)$ redundant scan it replaced ($n=61$, arm B; one contaminated $P=15$ launch, inflated across all kernels, is excluded). A 1.7$\times $ faster primitive leaves the kernel unchanged within 5\%.}}{27}{figure.caption.45}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces The vertical sweep: measured speedup of cache-blocked matrix powers across $R_v$. The projected curve is an explicit model claim, drawn dashed, never presented as data.}}{28}{figure.caption.47}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces The no-halo diagnostic. L2 tiling recovers toward baseline without the halo (the halo trade is the shortfall); L3 tiling barely moves (the cap is insensitive to cache residency).}}{28}{figure.caption.48}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces The two roofs on the block width $s$: the numerical certificate and the ghost-zone capacity, per tiling level.}}{29}{figure.caption.50}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {17}{\ignorespaces The regime map. The real Black--Scholes operator's refinement trajectory travels lower-right $\to $ lower-left $\to $ upper-left, crossing $\theta _v$ just under $n = 74$ and never entering the upper-right corner.}}{31}{figure.caption.52}%
